Boudewijn Waijers wrote:
> [Moria gives monster xp / player level for a kill]
> Translated to NetHack, this would mean that a grid bug would gain you only
> 1/30 experience point when you're at level 30 yourself... Of course, this
> would also mean that NetHack would have to use floating points...

No it wouldn't.  You simply store player experience points times player
level (multiply by new level, divide by old when it changes) and divide
whenever you need `real' experience points (or something more efficient
should it be necessary - the alternatives are fairly obvious).

This way, you simply increment by the unadjusted value of the monsters.

